# Evaluation Rules

When editing `eval/`:

## Stack

- **Library:** music21 (Python) for symbolic analysis
- **Metrics:** Harmonic Error Rate (HER), Repair Efficiency, CSI, SUS, NPS

## Commands

Use the Makefile to run evaluation. Do not hallucinate ad-hoc commands:

- `make calc-her` — Harmonic Error Rate benchmarking (0% parallel fifths, voice-crossing target)
- `make test-solver` — Solver/engine unit tests (via pytest or equivalent)
- `make eval-telemetry` — Repair Efficiency, survey data analysis

## HER Targets (PRD)

| Metric | Target |
|--------|--------|
| Parallel fifths | 0% |
| Voice-crossing | 0% |
| Latency-Utility | < 4 minutes to performance-ready |

Evaluation scripts consume MusicXML output from the engine. They do not invoke the LLM layer.